# Pin LF, for the same reason engine-rig/.gitattributes does: this host has
# core.autocrlf enabled, so without this git rewrites every checked-out line
# ending to CRLF. That would (a) make the jsonl datasets non-byte-reproducible
# across machines and (b) turn verify.py red on a fresh clone, since it treats
# CRLF in a dataset as an error.
#
# Found the way these things are always found: `git add` printed
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on the first commit of this territory.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
